The organisation can continue its critical operations during a disruption, and it can restore its systems and data from backups.

== How to decide if this control is required

This control is required when the organisation runs IT or services that its business or its customers depend on. NIS2 requires business continuity, backup management, disaster recovery, and crisis management.

== How to implement

Make a business continuity and recovery plan. Set recovery targets for the critical operations, and define the backups and the crisis management. Define the emergency communications: how the crisis team communicates securely when the normal systems are not available. Test the recovery at least once a year.

